# Check every file out byte-for-byte as it is committed: git never converts
# line endings here, whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows' system
# config and GitHub's Windows runners set it to true, which rewrote LF files to
# CRLF on checkout, and the code style enforced in the build (.editorconfig,
# IDE0055) then failed on them. Most files are LF; the CRLF-committed ones are
# declared in .editorconfig. Pinned by Infrastructure/CheckoutLineEndingsTests.
* -text
